/// @title Tenor
/// @author David Dada <daveproxy80@gmail.com> (https://github.com/dadadave80)
/// @notice The Tenor diamond: Lattice's initializer-guarded EIP-2535 proxy under Tenor's own name, owned by the
///         account that creates it. Every function it serves is a facet cut in by {initialize}.
/// @dev {Lattice-initialize} is first-caller-wins, and creating then initializing a diamond from a script takes two
///      transactions. The constructor records the deployer as owner through diamond-lib's {OwnableLib}, and
///      {initialize} accepts only that owner, so nobody can install a cut in between.
///      The owner slot keeps the deployer permanently. No facet in Tenor's current cut reads it, so today it gates
///      nothing but {initialize}. Cutting in a facet that checks {OwnableLib} — `OwnableFacet`, `DiamondCutFacet`,
///      `VestingWallet` — would make the deployer an authority outside AccessControl. Upgrades go through
///      `AccessControlDiamondCut` and its roles.
contract Tenor is Lattice {
    constructor() {
        OwnableLib.initializeOwner(msg.sender);
    }

    /// @notice Apply the initial facet cut and run the init delegatecall — owner only, and only once.
    /// @dev Reverts `Unauthorized()` for any caller but the owner, before Lattice's `initializer` guard runs.
    /// @param _facetCuts The initial facet cuts to install.
    /// @param _init The initializer contract delegatecalled after the cut (or address(0)).
    /// @param _calldata The delegatecall payload for `_init`.
    function initialize(FacetCut[] calldata _facetCuts, address _init, bytes calldata _calldata)
        public
        payable
        virtual
        override
    {
        OwnableLib.checkOwner();
        super.initialize(_facetCuts, _init, _calldata);
    }
}
